# Every deadline in the main sources, judged: tools/check/deadline-sites.py says what a site is and what each verdict
# means. <path> | <function> | <form> | <count> | <verdict> | <reason>. The question for each: what happens when the
# deadline fires as the bounded work returns (the timeout lands on another thread after the block returned and before
# the timeout's scope completed)? A new site, or one more in a function, fails until it is judged here.
kuicksilver-bench/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/bench/MemoryBench.kt | endpointIdle | withTimeout | 3 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result (the third only polls the cores' idle records)
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | awaitAnswer | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the stream's answered Deferred; the caller goes on either way, the answer stays in the stream
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | closeWithinBound | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a transport whose close completed as the bound fires is closed hard, and closeTransportOnce does nothing to a closed one
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | runHealthCheck | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | a PING acknowledgement read as the bound fires is taken from acked.isCompleted, not from the dropped result (CHANGELOG: "a health PING answered as its bound fires keeps the connection")
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | timerLoop | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the kick only wakes the loop, which reads the core's timers again on every turn; a kick dropped at the deadline is not needed
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | waitWithin | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | moved is set as the wait returns: a window or written frame taken as the send-stall bound fires is progress, not a stall
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/connectudp/UdpProxyImpl.kt | openSocket | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | only joins the factory call, which stores its outcome in slot; the caller decides ownership by one compareAndSet on slot after the deadline, so a socket stored as the deadline fires is the request's, and one stored after it is closed by the call
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.control.kt | readUni | timer | 1 | made-flag | the timer reads header.settled, which the reader sets when the type arrived; a header read as the timer fires is kept
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.critical.kt | attemptUntilTheLimitIsLow | timer | 1 | completedWithin | the attempt stores its result before it returns, and the guard's cancel gives the stored result (the same store-before-return)
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.kt | withinWtDeadline | select-cancel | 1 | completedWithin | the timer branch joins the cancelled block and returns its result when it completed all the same (CHANGELOG: "the WebTransport deadline keeps a CONNECT that completed after it was chosen")
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.shutdown.kt | goAwayConfined | timer | 1 | made-flag | rejects only the heads still pending with the same reader; a head read meanwhile left pendingHeaders and is the application's
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/RequestStream.kt | handOver | select-cancel | 1 | side-effect-free | a flush cancelled because the transport closed: nothing is taken from anyone, and a flush that completed first is left as it is
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/ServerRequestStream.kt | readRequestStream | timer | 1 | made-flag | the head timer acts only while head.settled is false; the reader settles the head as it arrives, so a head read in time is kept
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | endConnect | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the capsule reader for the peer's FIN; peerFinished is read after the wait, not the dropped result (the writes use completedWithin since class-sweep)
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | ended | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the capsule reader before terminate, which runs either way
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | watchConnectStopped | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | waits for the session's end that the capsule reader may decide; terminate runs after the wait and the first end wins, so a result dropped as the deadline fires changes nothing
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/H3Interop.kt | download | withTimeout | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/H3Interop.kt | download | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound on the client's closeAndJoin before the process exits: a close that completed as the bound fires was a join, a fired bound only logs; the download's result is already decided
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/HqInteropClient.kt | download | withTimeout | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/HqInteropClient.kt | download | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound on the client's closeAndJoin before the process exits: a close that completed as the bound fires was a join, a fired bound only logs; the download's result is already decided
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/Main.kt | serveUntilStopped | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound on the stopped server's closeAndJoin: a close that completed as the bound fires was a join, and the plain close() after a fired bound does nothing more to endpoints already closing or closed; only the log line and the returned flag differ, nothing depends on them but the test
kuicksilver-interop/src/jvmMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/Platform.jvm.kt | installStopSignal | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the shutdown hook only waits for the closed Deferred, which the server completes after its own bounded close; the hook returns either way and the JVM halts
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/Errors.kt | awaitContent | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | arrived is set as the wait returns: data that arrived as the socket timeout fires is read, not a SocketTimeoutException
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/Inactivity.kt | within | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | a tick seen as the timeout fires is read again from the tick count (ticks.value) before the timeout counts; the settled flag decides who ends the block
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KeptWithin.kt | keptWithin | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | completedWithin | the helper itself: kept is set as the block returns, with no suspension point in between, so a result returned as the timeout fires is the result (completedWithin for a block that may give null)
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | awaitResolutions | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | made-flag | resolved is set inside the scope as the resolutions are read, so the connect timeout firing then (also as the scope completes) keeps them; the second wait only joins the record jobs, read after it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | checkNetwork | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | awaits the first network report, a Deferred that keeps it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | httpsUpgrade | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | made-flag | decided is set inside the scope as the upgrade is decided, so the connect timeout firing then (also as the scope completes) keeps it; the second wait only joins the query, read after it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | lookupQuietly | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | side-effect-free | a lookup whose answer is kept in dns; the result is not used here
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRace.kt | runRace | onTimeout | 1 | select-atomic | select of the HTTP/3 attempt's Deferred and the timeout: the Deferred keeps its outcome whichever clause wins
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProxyResolverWindows.kt | run | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | the call's Deferred is read after the wait: an answer that came as the bound fires is the answer, not Failed
