kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | shareSameAddress | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the other setups' Deferreds, which keep their outcome; match reads them after the wait
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | track | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | pure-wait | waits for an exchange's end and writes a GOAWAY; the results are not used
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | webSocket | withTimeoutOrNull | 4 | made-flag | line 1: the CONNECT's stream is kept by connect's keep callback inside its withContext, so a CONNECT answered as the connect timeout fires is used. The close steps after the server's end was read (completedWithin keeps that): the FIN, the drain after T2; the second close wait's drain, dropped as it fires, is followed by stopSending, which the QUIC core sends only for a receive half that still wants it (RecvStream.wantsStopSending): one read to its FIN sends nothing
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/HappyEyeballs.kt | timer | timer | 1 | side-effect-free | the attempt-delay timer only sends a race event; cancelled with the race, it takes nothing
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/SocketTls.kt | close | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a socket job that completed as the bound fires gets abortTls, which does nothing to a closed session
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/SocketTls.kt | failTls | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the steps after a fatal alert (flush, pumps, linger, close); null aborts what is ending anyway
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/SocketTls.kt | lingerAfterAlert | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | discards the peer's bytes after an alert; they are not wanted
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/WebSocketPongs.kt | holdEnd | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | made-flag | the first only waits for peerDone; whether the end goes in order is read from peerEndedInOrder (set by the peer's Close or its end in order), or from the wait having run out, not from a result dropped as the bound fires. The second bounds the end after a cancellation, also its wait for the lock: an end that completed as it fires marked itself done in endHeld's finally, and the outer finally marks the held end ended (markEnded) whether endHeld ran or not, so the wait for it always ends
