kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/TcpListener.kt | withTimeoutOrRelease | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | made is set inside the block and released when the deadline fired: a TLS handshake that completes as the request-head deadline fires ends the connection. Kept, it would get what is left of that deadline (counted from accept), about nothing: an HTTP/2 preface gets no time, and an HTTP/1.1 head already buffered could still parse before that zero-delay timer, so keeping it would at most serve, at the deadline, a request the deadline refuses now; both ends are the deadline's to choose
